 Information printed out every QMC report loop:

 Shift: the energy offset calculated at the end of the report loop.
 Trace: The current total population on the diagonal elements of the first replica of the density matrix.
 Trace 2: The current total population on the diagonal elements of the second replica of the density matrix.
 Full S2: The numerator of the estimator for the Renyi entropy of the full system.
 \sum\rho_{ij}H_{ji}: The numerator of the estimator for the expectation value of the energy.
 \sum\rho_{ij}H2{ji}: The numerator of the estimator for the expectation value of the energy squared.
 \sum\rho_{ij}S_{ji}: The numerator of the estimator for the expectation value of the spin correlation function.
 \sum\rho_{ij}M2{ji}: The numerator of the estimator for the expectation value of the staggered magnetisation.
 RDM(n) S2: The numerator of the estimator for the Renyi entropy of RDM n.
 RDM(n) trace m: The current total population on the diagonal of replica m of RDM n.
 # particles: current total population of Hamiltonian particles.
 # states: number of many-particle states occupied.
 # spawn_events: number of successful spawning events across all processors.
 R_spawn: average rate of spawning across all processors.
 time: average time per Monte Carlo cycle.

 Note that all particle populations are averaged over the report loop.

